// The handpose package: five fingers that can hold, turn, press and knead. A
// program reaches it with 'import handpose'.
//
// WHAT IT IS. A hand as data (the lengths and thicknesses of its fingers, its
// palm), a pose of it (25 joint angles), and the three things that make a
// hand pick up a thing:
//
//   1. GRIP SHAPES: pairs of poses, a preshape and a closed shape (power, pinch,
//      hook, flat palm, claw), the standard taxonomy of prehensile grasps
//      (Napier 1956; Cutkosky 1989).
//   2. CONTACT: closing the fingers on a prop until they touch it and stop,
//      segment by segment, so that fingers wrap a handle and never pass through
//      it (the auto-grasp of GraspIt!, Miller and Allen 2004). A prop is any
//      surface that answers a signed distance: primitives, unioned. (grip.cone,
//      shape.cone)
//   3. PLACEMENT AND TASKS: putting the wrist where a handle needs it, from the
//      handle's data (its axis, radius, where along it, which side); and tasks as
//      cycles of wrist and finger motion (hold, turn, swing, press, knead) that
//      blend into one another. The arm follows by poseik's 'reachHand' through
//      'reachWrist'. (task.cone, reach.cone)
//
// The hand's fingers can be added as bones to a bonepose skeleton under its
// hand bone ('attachHand'), and a procedural hand to draw (testhand.cone) skins
// to them, so what is drawn is what the solver touched.
//
// FRAME: the hand bone's, bonepose's humanoid: the wrist at the origin, the fingers
// along -y, the right palm facing -x, the thumb on the -z side.
//
//   spec.cone      HandSpec, FingerSpec and HandPose: the hand as data
//   pose.cone      forward kinematics, the hand's bones, the stock poses
//   shape.cone     a prop's surface as signed distance primitives
//   grip.cone      grip shapes, closing on contact, placement on a handle, the pinch
//   task.cone      motions, tasks, the blend, evaluating a key against a prop
//   reach.cone     the arm to the wrist's place
//   testhand.cone  a procedural skinned hand, and the demo's props

mod handpose;

import libc;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import bonepose use *;
import poseik use *;
import mesh use Mesh;
